  ],
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>The equation of a plane passing through a point&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow></mfenced></math>&nbsp;and having direction ratios of the normal to the plane as&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#60;</mo><mi>a</mi><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>b</mi><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>c</mi><mo>&#62;</mo></math>&nbsp;is&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>a</mi><mfenced><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow></mfenced><mo>+</mo><mi>b</mi><mfenced><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>-</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow></mfenced><mo>+</mo><mi>c</mi><mfenced><mrow><mi>z</mi><mo>-</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo></math></p><p>Thus, the equation of the plane passing through <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></mfenced></math>&nbsp;is<br /><math><mi>a</mi><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></mfenced><mo>+</mo><mi>b</mi><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfenced><mo>+</mo><mi>c</mi><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi>z</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math></p><p><math><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi>a</mi><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>b</mi><mi>y</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>c</mi><mi>z</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>b</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8757;</mo></math> It passes through <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>&#160;</mi><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>&#160;</mi><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfenced></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi>c</mi><mo>=</mo><mo>-</mo><mi>b</mi></math></p><p><math><mo>&#8756;</mo></math> Equation of plane is&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>a</mi><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>b</mi><mi>y</mi><mo>-</mo><mi>b</mi><mi>z</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>b</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#8230;</mo><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mi>i</mi></mfenced></math></p><p><math><mo>&#8757;</mo></math> It makes angle <math><mfrac><mrow><mi>&#960;</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>4</mn></mrow></mfrac></math> with plane <math><mi>y</mi><mo>-</mo><mi>z</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>5</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math></p><p>The angle&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>&#952;</mi></math> between the planes&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>b</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mi>y</mi><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>c</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mi>z</mi><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math>&nbsp;and&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>b</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mi>y</mi><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>c</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mi>z</mi><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math>&nbsp;is defined as&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>cos</mi><mi>&#952;</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mfenced close=\"|\" open=\"|\"><mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>b</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><msub><mi>b</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>c</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><msub><mi>c</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></mfenced><mrow><msqrt><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>+</mo><msubsup><mi>b</mi><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>+</mo><msubsup><mi>c</mi><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup></msqrt><mo>&#215;</mo><msqrt><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>+</mo><msubsup><mi>b</mi><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>+</mo><msubsup><mi>c</mi><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup></msqrt></mrow></mfrac></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi>cos</mi><mrow><mfrac><mi>&#960;</mi><mn>4</mn></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mfenced close=\"|\" open=\"|\"><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>b</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow></mfenced><mrow><msqrt><msup><mi>a</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>b</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>b</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></msqrt><mo>&#215;</mo><msqrt><mn>2</mn></msqrt></mrow></mfrac></mrow></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msqrt><mn>2</mn></msqrt></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mfenced close=\"|\" open=\"|\"><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi>b</mi></mrow></mfenced><mrow><msqrt><msup><mi>a</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><msup><mi>b</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></msqrt><mo>&#215;</mo><msqrt><mn>2</mn></msqrt></mrow></mfrac></math></p><p>Squaring both sides, we get</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><msup><mi>a</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><msup><mi>b</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>4</mn><msup><mi>b</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><msup><mi>a</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><msup><mi>b</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi>a</mi><mo>=</mo><mo>&#177;</mo><msqrt><mn>2</mn></msqrt><mi>b</mi></math></p><p><math><mo>&#8756;</mo></math> Equation of plane is&nbsp;<math><mo>&#177;</mo><mi>&#160;</mi><msqrt><mn>2</mn></msqrt><mi>b</mi><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>b</mi><mi>y</mi><mo>-</mo><mi>b</mi><mi>z</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>b</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn><mi>&#160;</mi></math></p><p><math><mo>&#8658;</mo><mo>&#177;</mo><msqrt><mn>2</mn></msqrt><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>-</mo><mi>z</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math></p><p><math><mo>&#8756;</mo></math> Option <math><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><msqrt><mn>2</mn></msqrt><mo>,</mo><mi>&#160;</mi><mi>&#160;</mi><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>&#160;</mi><mn>4</mn></mrow></mfenced></math> satisfies the given equation.</p>"
  }
}